A||N||6||308||CRUISE CONTROL TROUBLE SHOOTING||||5||
Z||000000||308||09-09-2001||11:57 PM||||I am trying to fix my cruise control, I took off the vac canister and blew air in the Vac line under water and air came out the other port. From what I understand that means this is bad, Is this true.<P>I am also trying to find out if that's bad where can I get a new one and are they reasonable (I heard to get a plastic one)<P>If I replace this does it usually do the trick or does somthing else go wrong when the canister goes out. <P>Thanks in advance for any help.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||308||09-10-2001||12:15 AM||||I also forgot to ask, how do you check the switches on the Pedals (clutch & Brake) to see if they are good, Also is there a way to check the Cruise Stalk ||||reg||5
Z||000002||SLYGUY||09-10-2001||01:05 AM||||308...<BR>The cruise is out on my 88GT also. I dunno if it is in the stalk, or if it is a vacuum problem. I think I'm just gonna have my local Pontiac place fix it. I'll keep checking too see if anyone has any good advice.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||09-10-2001||09:29 AM||||The factory manual has several pages on diagnosing Cruise Control so it's a little hard to give a quick answer.<P>The clutch switch being out of adjustment was the problem on mine and I've heard it was on others. It has a yellow wire and a brown wire running to it. It should be closed when the pedal is up. A quick check would be to pull up on the pedal with your foot while driving and see if the cruise works. If you have a test light or meter unplug the wires and check for continuity while pushing the pedal in and out. It adjust by screwing the whole switch in or out of the bracket.<P>According to the wiring diagram there are 2 brake switches. Both need to be closed for the cruise to work. One has a yellow and a yellow/black wire. The other has a gray and a yellow (manual) or brown (auto).||||reg||1
Z||000004||TooManyFieros||09-10-2001||02:10 PM||||Somewhere on the net, there is a site where the guy has a real nice explaniation of how to trouble shoot the system. I think his name was Oliver Schotz in Germany. Here are some other links. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/diag.cruise-control.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/diag.cruise-control.html</A>           and      chech this out. Just click on the part with the mouse and you get info. <A HREF="http://www.members.tripod.com/fierodough/localrepair.htm." TARGET=_blank>http://www.members.tripod.com/fierodough/localrepair.htm.</A>     Good luck.<BR>    Jim||||reg||1
